<title>USA: Freddie Mac to redeem debenture issues.</title>
<headline>Freddie Mac to redeem debenture issues.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Home Loan Mortgage Corp said Monday that on November 19 it will redeem six debenture issues totalling $360 million, as follows.</p>
<p>		    Interest    Maturity</p>
<p>    Principal     Rate	  Date	   Cusip</p>
<p>  $100 million    6.23	09/25/98     3134AOLQ3</p>
<p>  $100 million    6.28	10/02/98     3134A0LV2</p>
<p>  $ 50 million    6.44	04/02/99     3134A0YY2</p>
<p>  $ 45 million    6.26	10/09/98     3134A0MY5</p>
<p>  $ 45 million    6.25	10/30/98     3134AOPK2</p>
<p>  $ 20 million    6.26	10/02/98     3134A0LX8</p>
<p>Freddie Mac said it will redeem the debenture issues in their entirety at a price equal to 100 percent of principal.</p>
<p>It said it will pay principal on the debentures along with interest accrued on the principal amount to the redemption date to holders of record as of the close of business on November 18.</p>
</text>
